identifier: kgmicrobe.compound:sodium_sulfite_pentahydrate
preferred_term: Na2SO3 x 5 H2O
ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: CHEBI:86477
  ontology_label: sodium sulfite
  ontology_source: CHEBI
  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: CultureMech
    notes: Imported from CultureMech pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#321)
    notes: molecular_formula '2Na.O3S' -> '2Na.O3S.5H2O'. The recorded value described
      the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by
      18 g/mol per water. Corrected because the label states 5 water(s) of hydration,
      and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous parent CHEBI:86477's
      ChEBI formula ('2Na.O3S') — the mark of a value inherited from the parent rather
      than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated notation.
  - evidence_type: LLM_SUGGESTION
    source: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1353.pdf
    notes: DSMZ1353 explicitly states Na2SO3 x5H2O0.01g in its500mL trace-element
      recipe. Preserve this source-stated five-water substance with its own registry
      identity and asymmetric sodium-sulfite parent under MAPPING_SEMANTICS§3; this
      is formal source transcription, not measured crystal-phase, commercial purity
      or supplier characterization. Exact current ChEBI query returned no hydrate
      term; PubChem19790054 has matching formal composition but the inspected synonym
      response supplies no CAS. No new CAS or molecular mass is asserted. The existing26
      occurrence statistics and all original histories are preserved; those26 occurrences,
      the inherited unqualified disodium-sulfite alias and downstream source/SSSOM
      selectors require their own scoped review. This proposal neither reassigns them
      nor clears their holds. Earlier database-match entries remain historical evidence
      of import/formula repair; they do not establish exact anhydrous identity.
synonyms:
- synonym_text: Anhydrous sodium sulfite
  synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL
  source: kg_microbe
- synonym_text: Sodium sulfite anhydrous
  synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL
  source: kg_microbe
- synonym_text: disodium sulfite
  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM
  source: chebi_synonym_review
mapping_status: MAPPED
occurrence_statistics:
